[{:db/id "q-84822/selection/6565259d757ba5ae59a9ca268bc35d4347b04edb06b424e6ceccb00790d82520" :answer/id #uuid "8a5b3f33-12a2-556c-b69c-8fc039817cc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4=-4t,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84822/selection/10014cefa2339e893149d6dcd8255da069d1f65071f2089d1bb08f04b2210e4f" :answer/id #uuid "aaf02e36-db8b-556d-a1d9-932359ceef98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4=-4t,\\,y+1=-2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84822/selection/c9e64c9ccf5b0317b2270c13cc3a4a07b2afd1ef927eedbb7b1b635faea793ed" :answer/id #uuid "118182d5-98b7-5d39-b306-f6fa747972e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4=-4t,\\,y-1=-2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84822/selection/90797255e7a2bcf8267b8e4dec04614c82b7fbe542742dcc44411986818c7045" :answer/id #uuid "18666983-92bc-5d49-b058-32873deb7b00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4=-t,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84822/selection/e07b247d9eaa020942ca1f0608a3266e7054cb18312e3341a3e005a7ebd23c50" :answer/id #uuid "a43d2dac-12b0-586a-918c-59c5a0986bc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4=-t,\\,y-1=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84822/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da49ccce-4df5-5496-9bd2-9779aaf1a732" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84822/selection/10014cefa2339e893149d6dcd8255da069d1f65071f2089d1bb08f04b2210e4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-84822/selection/6565259d757ba5ae59a9ca268bc35d4347b04edb06b424e6ceccb00790d82520" "q-84822/selection/10014cefa2339e893149d6dcd8255da069d1f65071f2089d1bb08f04b2210e4f" "q-84822/selection/c9e64c9ccf5b0317b2270c13cc3a4a07b2afd1ef927eedbb7b1b635faea793ed" "q-84822/selection/90797255e7a2bcf8267b8e4dec04614c82b7fbe542742dcc44411986818c7045" "q-84822/selection/e07b247d9eaa020942ca1f0608a3266e7054cb18312e3341a3e005a7ebd23c50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84822" :question/id #uuid "d30c94fd-fa02-5be8-ad6f-2f4f9c02d497" :question/math-academy-id "q-84822" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/6fcaa861fe507057f42c2194931bbc4a76d42891265ab40465832338cd8b5f4f.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-4,-1),$ and passes through the point $(0,-3).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-4,-1),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+4=2pt,\\,y+1=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(0,-3),$ we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=-3$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=2pt \\\\ -2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+4=2(-2)t,\\,y+1=(-2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+4=-4t,\\,y+1=-2{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84822/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84822"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447/selection/921f031aac19880dae9553effdd107ea2954a0cc70d3b507aac47795bbb84bbe" :answer/id #uuid "835e0a1a-b723-5064-8e33-8987a3a18d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=t,\\,\\,y-2={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447/selection/7fe3bf729d87a52c22bfeed8ddf358889becdd607a0ec6709a04312a1cdca244" :answer/id #uuid "1d2c872a-7d0c-506f-9378-3d42b3eee454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=t,\\,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447/selection/bfc6949fe6c0b2257a9a5c7584e8ecd2bde77e515efbc15125ebdeb8a12445ff" :answer/id #uuid "8e36d544-da4c-5b38-a3f0-cea6d0790f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447/selection/a026be6d9c166de7905f20c2e42f578fbf7b4381c03b0b98504d2faa6b096ff1" :answer/id #uuid "6ecadcb3-f282-5d55-8bd9-2ec6296e661b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=2t,\\,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447/selection/575f466368387b05de718598938ba3043e70fab8669cbf25ee1a8e79d97316ff" :answer/id #uuid "ad394608-abcb-5de2-b5ff-e06516eabe0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=t,\\,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "904337e3-8d48-5969-92a8-aaf05b0b62b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106447/selection/575f466368387b05de718598938ba3043e70fab8669cbf25ee1a8e79d97316ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-106447/selection/921f031aac19880dae9553effdd107ea2954a0cc70d3b507aac47795bbb84bbe" "q-106447/selection/7fe3bf729d87a52c22bfeed8ddf358889becdd607a0ec6709a04312a1cdca244" "q-106447/selection/bfc6949fe6c0b2257a9a5c7584e8ecd2bde77e515efbc15125ebdeb8a12445ff" "q-106447/selection/a026be6d9c166de7905f20c2e42f578fbf7b4381c03b0b98504d2faa6b096ff1" "q-106447/selection/575f466368387b05de718598938ba3043e70fab8669cbf25ee1a8e79d97316ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106447" :question/id #uuid "fedc73e9-6bd7-5662-845d-cc5946c6553c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106447" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/4ac7f5cd3405e3839b829edc19c440c973521a0263f1aaa0a2f8245697779561.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-1,2),$ and passes through the point $(1,4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-1,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+1=2pt,\\,y-2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(1,4),$ we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2pt \\\\ 2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+1=2(\\frac{1}{2})t,\\,y-2=(\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+1=t,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455/selection/3a6bb9e6300eb5d373332397621669d9f29d8da3d753908474500699cf2b7480" :answer/id #uuid "b75efa1a-29cb-56b2-88d0-505084f1fd3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=2t,\\,\\,y-3={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455/selection/23a829ed8ba001faf02ba2dfcd17bfc1e9c4b60e3bc6a37da14ad69424c4145d" :answer/id #uuid "76a74879-e62a-5db9-bd67-4c17732534c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=4t,\\,\\,y-3=4{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455/selection/118ec0fc8423fb96bddcd66f8c751a067c4fa8f31756ae67cb7c282f43e72b69" :answer/id #uuid "fa57c197-4d9c-5c03-96f0-8a7bead8fcd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=4t,\\,\\,y-3=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455/selection/ad3034c57a97d9da295dc9f6d2277bf79e26a3745b0d81fee9d34de09bf98bdc" :answer/id #uuid "792a5ae4-4af3-59c8-84a1-7dc28471f787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=4t,\\,\\,y+3=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455/selection/acf56bc8b213010f8cf1eba47225988380f4e305aaa018bddd53816e1be4e974" :answer/id #uuid "c2f086ac-b5c1-584f-9053-363ffda12355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=2t,\\,\\,y+3={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1e4cfb-2b12-591a-a043-70d77182305d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106455/selection/118ec0fc8423fb96bddcd66f8c751a067c4fa8f31756ae67cb7c282f43e72b69" :answer-field/choices ["q-106455/selection/3a6bb9e6300eb5d373332397621669d9f29d8da3d753908474500699cf2b7480" "q-106455/selection/23a829ed8ba001faf02ba2dfcd17bfc1e9c4b60e3bc6a37da14ad69424c4145d" "q-106455/selection/118ec0fc8423fb96bddcd66f8c751a067c4fa8f31756ae67cb7c282f43e72b69" "q-106455/selection/ad3034c57a97d9da295dc9f6d2277bf79e26a3745b0d81fee9d34de09bf98bdc" "q-106455/selection/acf56bc8b213010f8cf1eba47225988380f4e305aaa018bddd53816e1be4e974"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106455" :question/id #uuid "cbfcd767-3d5f-5cb8-8eab-0b33a201040a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106455" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(3,3)$ and which passes through the point $(7,5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(3,3),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-3=2pt,\\,y-3=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(7,5),$ we can substitute $x=7$ and $y=5$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=2pt \\\\ 2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2}{p} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-3=2(2)t,\\,y-3=(2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-3=4t,\\,y-3=2{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106455/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452/selection/83700b3ce379e41601713d4c74b3ec5897ac47906fd7c8883a3db511da850630" :answer/id #uuid "73d5206d-fdbf-580d-ab23-fa43572f6fd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=5t,\\,\\,y+3=-2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452/selection/771f818e26a7f123b3039c858dfa77028228c76626a45d3dac4dda0d1afac53a" :answer/id #uuid "258895d0-7b61-57ed-9571-b5c3ac4f8ea7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=-5t,\\,\\,y+3=-\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452/selection/99908ca73c6912dfe0f041fad6530ad9b45184ee2ba908b0c29d0ac8b6bfe435" :answer/id #uuid "695f8cd3-739e-5183-bcb5-ddaf72274d5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=-10t,\\,\\,y+3=-5{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452/selection/7f85e818e8493b27759cdd6424a231e86e95e219cec9416bcddf78e81deb9175" :answer/id #uuid "d0b852c5-550f-595e-98d5-79ff3935f2ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=-\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,\\,y+3=-\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452/selection/6ede373675bb7ac4d94ef8a29fd7a5c88bd85be9f274c8017b1efe587642c6cb" :answer/id #uuid "6f9a4fa1-d8c3-588f-98fe-b81a5881a397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=5t,\\,\\,y+3=\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "147672d7-0c0c-5a02-8cf9-6d414ff2f3b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106452/selection/771f818e26a7f123b3039c858dfa77028228c76626a45d3dac4dda0d1afac53a" :answer-field/choices ["q-106452/selection/83700b3ce379e41601713d4c74b3ec5897ac47906fd7c8883a3db511da850630" "q-106452/selection/771f818e26a7f123b3039c858dfa77028228c76626a45d3dac4dda0d1afac53a" "q-106452/selection/99908ca73c6912dfe0f041fad6530ad9b45184ee2ba908b0c29d0ac8b6bfe435" "q-106452/selection/7f85e818e8493b27759cdd6424a231e86e95e219cec9416bcddf78e81deb9175" "q-106452/selection/6ede373675bb7ac4d94ef8a29fd7a5c88bd85be9f274c8017b1efe587642c6cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106452" :question/id #uuid "3de3f5ae-3fc0-5c32-b996-56050a6bc315" :question/math-academy-id "q-106452" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/0c37bb9e010bdb19de2afc8707b6cf1cef69638c9f4721c407c1593f3a387b87.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-2,-3),$ and passes through the point $(-12,-13).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-2,-3),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+2=2pt,\\,y+3=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-12,-13),$ we can substitute $x=-12$ and $y=-13$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-10=2pt \\\\ -10=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10 & =2pt \\\\ -5 & =pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{5}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10 & =p{(-\\frac{5}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -10 & =p\\cdot \\frac{25}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -10 & =\\frac{25}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+2=2(-\\frac{5}{2})t,\\,y+3=(-\\frac{5}{2}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+2=-5t,\\,y+3=-\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106452/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106452"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824/selection/81e1784999c951e4d2db11441dea229ded6d9eb01d0834c54b0146db8cb37e70" :answer/id #uuid "4f7e0a0f-10e0-512f-a9ba-22366a5e9d97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=4t,\\,y-2=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824/selection/e0636bb6a519a621a5cb984f15b2a50304a384e358d6c5e5715e9a25d7794dc1" :answer/id #uuid "c2a57fb0-cad7-5588-b8d3-d730ff66eb23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=2t,\\,y+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824/selection/2c1ec85c8253438e7b5943b377c84c0c23303ec0965c661b6a3ff7539068d32b" :answer/id #uuid "d4742fad-09e4-509e-ad94-dee59336456e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=2t,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824/selection/4306b2e8423ae62596517e00bb52ed50a1b1356986db5e781398b73b217f60a0" :answer/id #uuid "650a6ce7-9b00-530b-90ae-d297f7b59a93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=2t,\\,y-2=4{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824/selection/38a6d0fbd3c4e4b93eac58879f80b055d9d1c254a8fc7816b4c8f56afe4823e2" :answer/id #uuid "219adf0c-dfc0-5f77-a8d8-4fb1806d2dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=4t,\\,y+2=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26302cf4-c209-56b7-bbed-7f797557ba1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84824/selection/81e1784999c951e4d2db11441dea229ded6d9eb01d0834c54b0146db8cb37e70" :answer-field/choices ["q-84824/selection/81e1784999c951e4d2db11441dea229ded6d9eb01d0834c54b0146db8cb37e70" "q-84824/selection/e0636bb6a519a621a5cb984f15b2a50304a384e358d6c5e5715e9a25d7794dc1" "q-84824/selection/2c1ec85c8253438e7b5943b377c84c0c23303ec0965c661b6a3ff7539068d32b" "q-84824/selection/4306b2e8423ae62596517e00bb52ed50a1b1356986db5e781398b73b217f60a0" "q-84824/selection/38a6d0fbd3c4e4b93eac58879f80b055d9d1c254a8fc7816b4c8f56afe4823e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84824" :question/id #uuid "c739ca25-5d75-5711-8097-97fe57c475b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-84824" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/bb83d1803b8b81992b8ed3f93019088beaba6db0fccf7ab707f03c55ed308678.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-1,2),$ and passes through the point $(-5,4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-1,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+1=2pt,\\,y-2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,4),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4=2pt \\\\ 2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2pt \\\\ -2 & =pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(-\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+1=2(2)t,\\,y-2=(2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+1=4t,\\,y-2=2{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84824/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460/selection/9126e60c31c758cbdd5e36e68ed552f33903141211c6299a7b8ca7947052abf2" :answer/id #uuid "e6d413c9-bc84-50ff-ba3f-ca7e5422b364" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460/selection/c8c61bbc1fbc1ecd23101529a5ea5a91277b37871514a3c244494269e48b8114" :answer/id #uuid "52281f8a-11f8-5a0b-942a-8477aca8faa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5=6{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+3=3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460/selection/8ea4a64629899470e458afca73b006311ce07bb30c2586612a9eb54d746c6e0d" :answer/id #uuid "cdb78dab-6fb8-5638-8472-2e7c7e5f3c4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5=3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+3=6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460/selection/1e154cc7c9d75ca24cb7a1fcbd3cc5941aa634e72e35bba656a1d2920006970e" :answer/id #uuid "ac2dd016-0425-5d40-ad73-06dd0e16f843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=6t,\\,\\,y+5=3{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460/selection/19418e1a6d0a7977209526fd54daa14326f2468f49cd9ccac4fb749303eb50d1" :answer/id #uuid "2db5ca93-30e8-5da6-990b-d8942febd9ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+3=-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77e16c48-9b1a-5f6d-9db8-0fd49008fb93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106460/selection/8ea4a64629899470e458afca73b006311ce07bb30c2586612a9eb54d746c6e0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-106460/selection/9126e60c31c758cbdd5e36e68ed552f33903141211c6299a7b8ca7947052abf2" "q-106460/selection/c8c61bbc1fbc1ecd23101529a5ea5a91277b37871514a3c244494269e48b8114" "q-106460/selection/8ea4a64629899470e458afca73b006311ce07bb30c2586612a9eb54d746c6e0d" "q-106460/selection/1e154cc7c9d75ca24cb7a1fcbd3cc5941aa634e72e35bba656a1d2920006970e" "q-106460/selection/19418e1a6d0a7977209526fd54daa14326f2468f49cd9ccac4fb749303eb50d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106460" :question/id #uuid "06a1eae4-f144-5f48-9020-f9d76a858d18" :question/math-academy-id "q-106460" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/c6496d117c1b769474c353b0bfeef6836d21f080fb108752d55b8bb090dc0243.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(-5,-3),$ and passes through the point $(7,9).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-5,-3),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+5=p{t}^{2},\\,y+3=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(7,9),$ we can substitute $x=7$ and $y=9$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 12=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =2pt \\\\ 6 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{6}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =p{(\\frac{6}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 12 & =p\\cdot \\frac{36}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{36}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+5=(3){t}^{2},\\,y+3=2(3)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+5=3{t}^{2},\\,y+3=6t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106460/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106460"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459/selection/3e4de2ffd76ba6f4a1846d3352112b0b4e619d25dc1f9dadd5be574339ebd8d9" :answer/id #uuid "d30c50bf-dcb4-5c95-89a2-20f6e65a20d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-3=2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459/selection/bafbf5e3acca9b43bdde8f6261530eb7de92c678ffd1c815357aa28dbc9a7afe" :answer/id #uuid "64a2e915-43f9-5524-8a15-aa424cb76d5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+3=4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459/selection/ba92fcbc1017a1513019a983589992a8931d18a8c3b31a8b6c36baacceffd60f" :answer/id #uuid "80b24bdc-0bbd-58b8-bcdb-240784c71cb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=4t,\\,\\,y+2=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459/selection/1ed8c4ea83697ad75acd98c998347a2e40e4540898039e7c296045987ac689e4" :answer/id #uuid "4b68f148-25b9-5e0e-903c-5cf5b6f424ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-3=4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459/selection/17ea2325d394bda7b1abea7cab6491a66e75fde718c848a1cc66f23beebc303f" :answer/id #uuid "8751437e-3810-5a6a-8fd5-be2296ef9a63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=-2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-3=-4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc168168-de42-55fb-977e-49bfcf0ca43e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106459/selection/1ed8c4ea83697ad75acd98c998347a2e40e4540898039e7c296045987ac689e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-106459/selection/3e4de2ffd76ba6f4a1846d3352112b0b4e619d25dc1f9dadd5be574339ebd8d9" "q-106459/selection/bafbf5e3acca9b43bdde8f6261530eb7de92c678ffd1c815357aa28dbc9a7afe" "q-106459/selection/ba92fcbc1017a1513019a983589992a8931d18a8c3b31a8b6c36baacceffd60f" "q-106459/selection/1ed8c4ea83697ad75acd98c998347a2e40e4540898039e7c296045987ac689e4" "q-106459/selection/17ea2325d394bda7b1abea7cab6491a66e75fde718c848a1cc66f23beebc303f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106459" :question/id #uuid "8ad81bfb-009f-58b8-9a49-7041a80190ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-106459" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/0e7558b9858668e619e3f7750efd76043981e2b833bcda7c7e462f6ecda1aa10.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(-2,3),$ and passes through the point $(6,11).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-2,3),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+2=p{t}^{2},\\,y-3=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(6,11),$ we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=11$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 8=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =2pt \\\\ 4 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{4}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =p{(\\frac{4}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 8 & =p\\cdot \\frac{16}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{16}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+2=(2){t}^{2},\\,y-3=2(2)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+2=2{t}^{2},\\,y-3=4t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106459/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465/selection/f443d802b09ed25f60682367f19c02119a1a45eb458f806b07f965e23468da4e" :answer/id #uuid "32999de3-d390-5e7b-8e44-6029adc7ac8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+3=-\\frac{1}{2}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465/selection/38435f027f521d197c54b3d92645bb991ac88200d7366e02d60479ebde563bf9" :answer/id #uuid "8823679c-4206-593e-9924-bba1b808b386" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-8t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465/selection/de72392754c02e30dae779dd4b4235df1951cdde086fadcf8cdde3d42b110c05" :answer/id #uuid "9f933ccb-75fa-51e5-b46c-a9bcbb9b8b57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465/selection/cebdc1297faec74271f2bce9439ffa44cc285efa0d45f8bf20e27a34f4881095" :answer/id #uuid "b8ce72c8-fabe-53b4-9353-dea6391c44b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465/selection/9dd4e8287025ae37791a72151600c7eabf7ec2faa1f4e21aee4c2bd8549de4f2" :answer/id #uuid "9445efe6-ebcf-5fed-8a56-5ce164ddda33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bd091d-91d9-5843-968d-693b832cddd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106465/selection/de72392754c02e30dae779dd4b4235df1951cdde086fadcf8cdde3d42b110c05" :answer-field/choices ["q-106465/selection/f443d802b09ed25f60682367f19c02119a1a45eb458f806b07f965e23468da4e" "q-106465/selection/38435f027f521d197c54b3d92645bb991ac88200d7366e02d60479ebde563bf9" "q-106465/selection/de72392754c02e30dae779dd4b4235df1951cdde086fadcf8cdde3d42b110c05" "q-106465/selection/cebdc1297faec74271f2bce9439ffa44cc285efa0d45f8bf20e27a34f4881095" "q-106465/selection/9dd4e8287025ae37791a72151600c7eabf7ec2faa1f4e21aee4c2bd8549de4f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106465" :question/id #uuid "efd48b95-db5f-52c0-99e2-d4c8610ebe36" :question/math-academy-id "q-106465" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y+1)^{2}=-(x-3)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(3,-1).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx-3=p{t}^{2},\\,y+1=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =-(x-3) \\\\ 4p(x-3) & =-(x-3) \\\\ 4p & =-1 \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-3=(-\\frac{1}{4}){t}^{2},\\,y+1=2(-\\frac{1}{4})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106465/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106465"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463/selection/0d8857a096bbd3748ce9696a74ce653ef01686b30bc48a660e5fb143b2884ffc" :answer/id #uuid "8e0eb2be-bc36-5cad-b102-f63bde897b30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5=-6t,\\,\\,y+2=-3{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463/selection/ec8221568edb927481d8d81de962812341a44ab1bfabdb00f1fff4773a396236" :answer/id #uuid "e0485994-9768-54ef-a94e-b9fc4f91eed2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+2=-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463/selection/a804c5810674ca3a854c40980ad43ac7a6f2b9853172ba0c79b952dedaf96c4d" :answer/id #uuid "70dc7a8d-0093-57c2-bb9c-4a6b44a79748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463/selection/0e476d65f279eed3072768bfed37673b8811f8940d3d19ec1730f31b1dee5bbc" :answer/id #uuid "6cd55ad8-4124-5733-9f0a-59af107645f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463/selection/6ce9f4ef6009537854689d119051452a4de4658b9844c26cc52fe83c63a52f01" :answer/id #uuid "83b5fd85-0f2d-57e9-a0c2-c598ef02e598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-5=-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef91dae4-9dde-5751-9c5f-7995f46057bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106463/selection/a804c5810674ca3a854c40980ad43ac7a6f2b9853172ba0c79b952dedaf96c4d" :answer-field/choices ["q-106463/selection/0d8857a096bbd3748ce9696a74ce653ef01686b30bc48a660e5fb143b2884ffc" "q-106463/selection/ec8221568edb927481d8d81de962812341a44ab1bfabdb00f1fff4773a396236" "q-106463/selection/a804c5810674ca3a854c40980ad43ac7a6f2b9853172ba0c79b952dedaf96c4d" "q-106463/selection/0e476d65f279eed3072768bfed37673b8811f8940d3d19ec1730f31b1dee5bbc" "q-106463/selection/6ce9f4ef6009537854689d119051452a4de4658b9844c26cc52fe83c63a52f01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106463" :question/id #uuid "659918a3-ff24-5f01-abd6-269b3bb800ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-106463" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/d7a5a3f962080fe457e5d35a581ee1340f1603f0c3bc64be4de6e7553f4402e1.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(2,-5),$ and passes through the point $(-5,-7).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(2,-5),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-2=p{t}^{2},\\,y+5=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-10,7),$ we can substitute $x=-10$ and $y=7$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-12=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 12=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =2pt \\\\ 6 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{6}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12 & =p{(\\frac{6}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -12 & =p\\cdot \\frac{36}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{36}{p} \\\\ p & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-2=(-3){t}^{2},\\,y+5=2(-3)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-2=-3{t}^{2},\\,y+5=-6t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106463/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847/selection/a4c01289ebc933fd068174a1ac90c99b36466293ab96681aa245bc5c36c93410" :answer/id #uuid "60b04aee-002e-58a0-9ffe-21f7b9716dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2={t}^{2},\\,y-6=2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847/selection/d2881332ba0dba84c1ea9948682f812b1d0ecb53bd2b3d1293cb4158ca740206" :answer/id #uuid "0e59acd3-3242-55d3-a9b7-19247f4e24e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+6=4{t}^{2},\\,y-2=8t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847/selection/60999129bedc87b87a2fdaa74c9bfcd8db5b5618b0fae572e0f83cbafde9ae0d" :answer/id #uuid "1b8f13af-e4cd-5fbd-8eaa-86720f166fe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-6=8{t}^{2},\\,y+2=4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847/selection/de30539ff37a11bd3daa0087247770fa0923de1408ba47c2fbf71e51e635501e" :answer/id #uuid "39229461-a248-58d8-bd33-5f6f795d0367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=4{t}^{2},\\,y+6=2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847/selection/37e4f184bd550f359e7c55eb1f5e1627f0cfa1aa8d284ed7f9dfa27d86c31342" :answer/id #uuid "481f85f8-bfe2-5199-a60f-cd2e3b0130d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+6=2{t}^{2},\\,y-2=4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da975536-095e-5181-8cb0-81f6b31aa0bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84847/selection/d2881332ba0dba84c1ea9948682f812b1d0ecb53bd2b3d1293cb4158ca740206" :answer-field/choices ["q-84847/selection/a4c01289ebc933fd068174a1ac90c99b36466293ab96681aa245bc5c36c93410" "q-84847/selection/d2881332ba0dba84c1ea9948682f812b1d0ecb53bd2b3d1293cb4158ca740206" "q-84847/selection/60999129bedc87b87a2fdaa74c9bfcd8db5b5618b0fae572e0f83cbafde9ae0d" "q-84847/selection/de30539ff37a11bd3daa0087247770fa0923de1408ba47c2fbf71e51e635501e" "q-84847/selection/37e4f184bd550f359e7c55eb1f5e1627f0cfa1aa8d284ed7f9dfa27d86c31342"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84847" :question/id #uuid "a45072fa-409b-5a6f-a637-083f290f0cb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-84847" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y-2)^{2}=16(x+6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-6,2).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx+6=p{t}^{2},\\,y-2=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =16(x+6) \\\\ 4p(x+6) & =16(x+6) \\\\ 4p & =16 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+6=(4){t}^{2},\\,y-2=2(4)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+6=4{t}^{2},\\,y-2=8t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84847/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-323153/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b7a9c3fe-b99a-57ac-b2b3-147b483ebeab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323153/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c1f56675-0ca9-546d-8c77-52d997de7ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323153/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "430e6a32-c5ac-536e-895d-3f04d1aa6890" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323153/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-323153/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-323153/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323153/field-2/d1b66a778537eeb276c41f3d6f79cc45c28fafa1ed9eed1198983c04ecbb5586" :answer/id #uuid "dbec2081-f15a-5ba0-aa49-e407ae6eddb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-y-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323153/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bb41120-1a14-5ab8-8ea6-dbbc84a01976" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323153/field-2/d1b66a778537eeb276c41f3d6f79cc45c28fafa1ed9eed1198983c04ecbb5586" :answer-field/choices ["q-323153/field-2/d1b66a778537eeb276c41f3d6f79cc45c28fafa1ed9eed1198983c04ecbb5586"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323153" :question/id #uuid "4eca1d59-0a7a-514c-be56-d9295bc3b025" :question/math-academy-id "q-323153" :question/problem "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola\n\n$$\nx-4=-\\frac{2}{5}\\,t,\\,y+1=-\\frac{4}{25}\\,{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{5}{2}(x-4),\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{25}{4}(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{5}{2}(x-4))}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}\\,(x-4)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{25}{4}(y+1)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{25}{4}\\,(x-4)^{2} & =-\\frac{25}{4}(y+1) \\\\ {(x-4)}^{2} & =-(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-323153/field-1" "q-323153/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-323153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503/selection/7dcdaddc5fd99eff421bb8a93d49431514156d2e8f018de24547a06971a95f2d" :answer/id #uuid "49983970-ecb2-5bca-bf85-b57a7c935a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}=-(y+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503/selection/e30ef462bf6c1b3dc4855ff5b1bac83d59dc21284a1d957fb436b712c1d20fd5" :answer/id #uuid "44be291b-ea6e-568e-8944-73e67ac5cb78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}(y+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503/selection/ae082d2363e712558e40e4ddf06ce893756dbd20702101d9c218e51b460d9be7" :answer/id #uuid "0c81681f-5e2a-5bf1-83b6-c8bc1d99c28e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}=(y+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503/selection/8893810c2c460e72daca7678d3523199df8a58b7e8df9f8fbbf0f99f9ffc40cf" :answer/id #uuid "5e96a228-acf3-54bb-8b82-104a11d94960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}=-(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503/selection/1a56af31d2f4714c6623873656d0edf7a0c1a3474511542ca224940e23f79664" :answer/id #uuid "0c3974bc-a350-519e-8ce6-ba96c263be60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}=-4(y+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "772154c2-b716-5c23-8f34-9f1a094aff9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106503/selection/7dcdaddc5fd99eff421bb8a93d49431514156d2e8f018de24547a06971a95f2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-106503/selection/7dcdaddc5fd99eff421bb8a93d49431514156d2e8f018de24547a06971a95f2d" "q-106503/selection/e30ef462bf6c1b3dc4855ff5b1bac83d59dc21284a1d957fb436b712c1d20fd5" "q-106503/selection/ae082d2363e712558e40e4ddf06ce893756dbd20702101d9c218e51b460d9be7" "q-106503/selection/8893810c2c460e72daca7678d3523199df8a58b7e8df9f8fbbf0f99f9ffc40cf" "q-106503/selection/1a56af31d2f4714c6623873656d0edf7a0c1a3474511542ca224940e23f79664"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106503" :question/id #uuid "90e7bbda-fedf-5ef5-9757-a13f2517bec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106503" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+2=-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y+3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-2(x+2),\\,{t}^{2}=-4(y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-2(x+2))}^{2} \\\\  & =4{(x+2)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-4(y+3)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x+2)}^{2} & =-4(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =-(y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106503/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106503"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854/selection/db77e4fece04429c7325172200d28d9b55386d18514984882a856e0c3453da65" :answer/id #uuid "bb6aaa2c-6bb8-5d0f-8dfb-ab79a6e5f6d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}=-2(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854/selection/2e31eafae4e32d895fa8ce69439dbfa256f84ccd71ae4bf094e7bdff6fd494a5" :answer/id #uuid "38917827-6af0-5c38-b487-5c5e1726bac6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}=4(y-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854/selection/23fab81caf62e8fb4702b0695e42fc40aa6bf41a56e472a066d5bcc8d71886db" :answer/id #uuid "32d0b6a3-4155-5e70-a0c7-78bc670f44d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}=8(y-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854/selection/79c2f77cfc3f468385a80dad8605e2d407aea17175dc2e53bb60a2415217ecbe" :answer/id #uuid "670b7ebf-f3db-5ec2-8cab-43a4597d1678" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}=-8(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854/selection/f63ef1040c5d868a82384cba06b56c8498dafea027e3a4638a8f4c2362edd465" :answer/id #uuid "9e7d2afa-4da0-578d-99be-a65c3d8f3e08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}=-4(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "94c9ce65-48b0-577b-9094-c99c3fb2fe40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84854/selection/f63ef1040c5d868a82384cba06b56c8498dafea027e3a4638a8f4c2362edd465" :answer-field/choices ["q-84854/selection/db77e4fece04429c7325172200d28d9b55386d18514984882a856e0c3453da65" "q-84854/selection/2e31eafae4e32d895fa8ce69439dbfa256f84ccd71ae4bf094e7bdff6fd494a5" "q-84854/selection/23fab81caf62e8fb4702b0695e42fc40aa6bf41a56e472a066d5bcc8d71886db" "q-84854/selection/79c2f77cfc3f468385a80dad8605e2d407aea17175dc2e53bb60a2415217ecbe" "q-84854/selection/f63ef1040c5d868a82384cba06b56c8498dafea027e3a4638a8f4c2362edd465"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84854" :question/id #uuid "0acf6f7c-0905-523f-bd2c-b81ada5c183d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84854" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+5=-2t,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x+5}{2},\\,{t}^{2}=-(y+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{x+5}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-(y+2)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{4} & =-(y+2) \\\\ (x+5)^{2} & =-4(y+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84854/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84854"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-323229/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "52ea6cc9-037b-5caf-8807-ba3a131db9ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323229/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f15f65c-b5da-5827-843f-3ab9389d9944" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323229/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-323229/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323229/field-2/29ecc15d116fbf9d10ffb761395531219cc764d7b0c6e06fcf49183f37b4b12e" :answer/id #uuid "68c4bc08-c537-579b-bd5c-6f88aa96796f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4x+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323229/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6304e4eb-2a97-5376-8811-3dcf21cea22e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323229/field-2/29ecc15d116fbf9d10ffb761395531219cc764d7b0c6e06fcf49183f37b4b12e" :answer-field/choices ["q-323229/field-2/29ecc15d116fbf9d10ffb761395531219cc764d7b0c6e06fcf49183f37b4b12e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323229" :question/id #uuid "9d85e680-26c7-5aac-9193-74809aef6804" :question/math-academy-id "q-323229" :question/problem "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx-3=-{t}^{2},\\,y+4=-2t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(y\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-(x-3),\\,t=-\\frac{y+4}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{y+4}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-(x-3)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4} & =-(x-3) \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-4(x-3) \\\\ {(y+4)}^{2} & =-4(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-323229/field-1" "q-323229/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-323229"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-323216/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c18fbe89-3cbf-5047-a7ca-2f741f7315c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323216/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "584ae79f-f0ff-5cc5-8c9c-d7676af6e402" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323216/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-323216/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323216/field-2/7137eb283ca8c0f12b58bf24ff02cb2945eae54efba7dd43f262d6f9672a1a20" :answer/id #uuid "7cebe2d5-9118-5944-8a19-b830c1b4b248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323216/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "512da331-1f37-5611-b546-300d3b7ef138" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323216/field-2/7137eb283ca8c0f12b58bf24ff02cb2945eae54efba7dd43f262d6f9672a1a20" :answer-field/choices ["q-323216/field-2/7137eb283ca8c0f12b58bf24ff02cb2945eae54efba7dd43f262d6f9672a1a20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323216" :question/id #uuid "63957822-af5c-5047-b47d-705f224584f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-323216" :question/problem "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y-3=5t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(y\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =x,\\,t=\\frac{y-3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{y-3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=x$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{25} & =x \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =25x \\\\ {(y-3)}^{2} & =25x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-323216/field-1" "q-323216/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-323216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7446"] :question/problem "What set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in(-\\infty, \\infty),$ generates the parabola shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/1a75a5242f3636efac8def7fc62458e1c1c6972ca79a1ab6fd73af47be622a7a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-4,5),$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx - h = 2pt, \\qquad y - k = pt^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k) = (-4,5),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx + 4 = 2pt, \\qquad y - 5 = pt^2.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-2, 3),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=3$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2pt \\\\ -2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx + 4 = 2\\left(-\\dfrac12\\right)t, \\qquad y - 5 = \\left(-\\dfrac12\\right)t^2 ,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx + 4 = -t, \\qquad y - 5 = -\\dfrac12t^2 .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7447"] :question/problem "What set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in(-\\infty,\\infty),$ generates the parabola shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/8355891fbc605593a32dd100ee8c1c2e4324da0630755984158ec23f6d419ab9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(-3,2),$ and passes through the point $(1,0).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx - h = pt^2, \\qquad y - k = 2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k) = (-3,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+3 = pt^2, \\qquad y-2 = 2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(1,0),$ we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=0$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=p{t}^{2} \\\\ -2=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =p{(-\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+3 = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right)t^2, \\qquad y -2 = 2\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right)t ,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+3 = \\dfrac{1}{4}t^2, \\qquad y -2= \\dfrac{1}{2}t .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7448"] :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-1 = -2t^2, \\qquad y+1 = -4t, \\qquad t\\in(-\\infty, \\infty).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-\\frac{x-1}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{y+1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{y+1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation $t^2 = -\\dfrac{x-1}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =-\\frac{x-1}{2} \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{x-1}{2}) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =-8(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
